analysisWe need to produce assert statement for the comment at end of previousClearBit method.

Comment: 
"@@@ If the starting index is greater than or equal to -1, then for every index greater than the result and less than or equal to the starting index, the bit at that index is set to true."

Interpretation: For method previousClearBit(int fromIndex) returns an int result (index of previous clear bit). The spec: If fromIndex >= -1, then for all i such that result < i <= fromIndex, the bit at i is true (i.e., set). Note: result could be -1 if none found. Also we must consider precondition: starting index >= -1. The method already throws if fromIndex < -1. So we can assert that if fromIndex >= -1 then for all i where \result < i && i <= fromIndex, get(i) == true.

We need to use this.get(i) method to check bit. So assert expression: (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i));

But need to ensure that get returns boolean, true means set. So condition is this.get(i). Also need to handle case when result == -1: then condition becomes -1 < i && i <= fromIndex, i.e., i from 0 to fromIndex inclusive. That's fine.

Thus final assert: assert (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i));.

Make sure syntax: parentheses around implication: (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i));

